      "writtenOn": "2024-11-26T10:59:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not familiar with the terminology used in UpdateEngine. What does `Stable` mean here? Isn\u0027t it a `Manager` class?\n\n\n\u003e This interface has lesser functionalities than UpdateEngine and doesn\u0027t allow cancel.\n\n`UpdateEngine` is @SystemApi. Why does `UpdateEngine` and  `UpdateEngineStable` need to be a separate class in the API surface?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 44,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 44,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "fixSuggestions": [
        {
          "fixId": "5a685f3a_14dc116f",
          "description": "prompt_to_edit API",
          "replacements": [
            {
              "path": "core/java/android/os/UpdateEngineStable.java",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 25,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 27,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": " * UpdateEngineStable handles calls to the update engine stable which takes care of A/B OTA updates\n * and is a part of the update engine service. This interface has lesser functionalities than\n * UpdateEngine and doesn\u0027t allow cancel.\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "revId": "06866f1db6385ef8ca464be9b41b717bf65827c7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9a5513d9_fb8d568c",
        "filename": "core/java/android/os/UpdateEngineStable.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 44,
      "author": {
        "id": 1710792
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-27T22:52:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "UpdateEngineStable predates my work on OTA, so I don\u0027t know why it is named as such. Not sure why two different AIDL definitions are needed, but `UpdateEngine.aidl` and `UpdateEngineStable.aidl` have different API surfaces and have different permission settings, hence they need to be different classes.",
      "parentUuid": "4768a36b_153d72c5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 44,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 44,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "06866f1db6385ef8ca464be9b41b717bf65827c7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "193245e3_1fc33914",
        "filename": "core/java/android/os/UpdateEngineStable.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 44,
      "author": {
        "id": 1710792
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-27T22:54:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "re difference between `UpdateEngine` and `UpdateEngineStable`\n\n`UpdateEngineStable` has less API surface, we generally prefer granting permission for `UpdateEngineStable` if possible. `UpdateEngine` is only meant for applications which manage OTA updates(for example GMSCore). Since The intended use case of this new API is only to optimize when postinstall scripts run, and do not intend to take part in OTA installation, we prefer to use `UpdateEngineStable`",
      "parentUuid": "9a5513d9_fb8d568c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 44,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 44,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "06866f1db6385ef8ca464be9b41b717bf65827c7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8cfb0aa9_669b32d5",
        "filename": "core/java/android/os/UpdateEngineStable.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 44,
      "author": {
        "id": 1047684
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-27T23:49:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIUC, normally, Android frameworks manager class checks the permission in the service side during a AIDL method call, and different methods require different permissions. Are you saying that the permission or uid is checked during `onBind()` instead, and 2 different permissions are needed to bind `UpdateEngineStable` and `UpdateEngine` respectively? Would it possible to document the permission with `@RequirePermission`?\n\nI can\u0027t find the documentation why it\u0027s called `stable` either. My speculation is that UpdateEngineStable seems to maintain a stable and versioned AIDL interface. Particularly, \n\n\u003e If a device is shipped with such a backward incompatible change, it has a high risk of breaking later when a module using the interface is updated, e.g., Mainline modules.` \n\nhttps://r.android.com/1371069\n\nShould ART just talk to UpdateEngineStable via AIDL instead via a frameworks API here?",
      "parentUuid": "193245e3_1fc33914",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 44,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 44,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "06866f1db6385ef8ca464be9b41b717bf65827c7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8922acd4_bb59b2eb",
